      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Sungtak. We fixed CTS to honor KEY_STRIDE/KEY_SLICE_HEIGHT for encoder ByteBuffer input, which fixes EncodeDecodeTest on our device. testEncoderQuality still failed, and we found the description gap you mentioned. For 320x240 COLOR_FormatYUV420Planar the wrapped input block\n  (c2.android and vendor encoders alike) has Y at 0 (rowInc 512), U at 122880 and V at 155648 (rowInc 256), while the format reports KEY_STRIDE\u003d512 / KEY_SLICE_HEIGHT\u003d240, which place V at 153600. The chroma plane height is padded from 120 to 128 rows. We\u0027re abandoning this CL in favor\n  of https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/frameworks/av/+/4430217, which wraps Planar/SemiPlanar/P010 only when the U/V offsets match the stride/slice-height layout, so padded strides and slice heights stay zero-copy. With it plus the CTS fix : https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/cts/+/4429480, all affected tests pass.\n\nCan you please help to review both the changes. Updating the same in Bug as well.",
